---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How FileLocker Works | Browser-Based File Protection" 
  description="Learn how FileLocker protects files directly in your browser. Discover how client-side processing and AES-GCM encryption keep your files 100% private."
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="guide-hero">
    <div class="hero-shape hero-shape-1"></div>
    <div class="hero-shape hero-shape-2"></div>
    <div class="hero-shape hero-shape-3"></div>
    <div class="hero-inner text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1>How FileLocker Works</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle max-w-xl mx-auto">
        FileLocker is designed so selected files are processed locally in your browser rather than uploaded to a FileLocker server. Here is what happens when you protect a file.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="w-full bg-white py-12 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

      <div class="content-card animate-fade-in-up">
        <h2 class="section-heading">How FileLocker Password Protection Works</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">FileLocker lets you password protect files and folders online while keeping the file-processing work in your browser. The workflow is simple: choose what you want to protect, create a password, encrypt the data, and save the resulting .vault file.</p>
        
        <ol class="steps-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
          <li class="step-card">
            <span class="step-number">1</span>
            <strong>Select a file or folder</strong>
            <span>When you click "Upload" or drag a file into FileLocker, we do not send it to a server. Instead, your web browser asks for permission to read the selected file locally on your device.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="step-card">
            <span class="step-number">2</span>
            <strong>Create a password</strong>
            <span>The password you enter is used by FileLocker to derive the cryptographic key used by its encryption process. The protected data cannot be decrypted through FileLocker without the correct password.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="step-card">
            <span class="step-number">3</span>
            <strong>Encrypt and build the .vault file</strong>
            <span>FileLocker processes your file chunk-by-chunk and writes the scrambled data into a new <code>.vault</code> file. Because this happens directly on your device, this approach can reduce memory pressure compared with loading the entire file at once. Practical limits still depend on your browser, device resources, and available storage.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="step-card">
            <span class="step-number">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
            </span>
            <strong>Save the protected file</strong>
            <span>Your browser will prompt you to save the resulting protected file. You can then email it, upload it to cloud storage, or put it on a USB drive. Anyone opening the protected file will need the correct password to decrypt it with our <a href="/unlock-file/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Unlock Tool</a>.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="content-card animate-fade-in-up animate-delay-1">
        <h2 class="section-heading">How FileLocker Handles Security & Cryptography</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">FileLocker uses PBKDF2/Argon2id key derivation and authenticated AES-GCM encryption to protect your data. Explore our complete technical write-up or read practical step-by-step guides for different file formats.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-2">
          <a href="/security/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Read the FileLocker security architecture →</a>
          <a href="/guides/how-to-password-protect-files/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Read the Master File Protection Guide →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="cta-banner mt-8 animate-fade-in-up animate-delay-2">
        <p class="cta-label">Ready to password protect your data?</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 relative z-10">
          <a href="/lock-file/" class="cta-button">Protect a File Now</a>
          <a href="/lock-folder/" class="cta-button" style="background:transparent;color:#fff;border:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.4);">Protect a Folder Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
